    "title": "Actor Bill Murray in attendance at UConn's Sweet 16 game",
    "text": "PHILADELPHIA, PENNSYLVANIA - MARCH 22: Actor Bill Murray in the stands during game between UCLA Bruins and UConn Huskies in the second half in the second round of the 2026 NCAA Men's Basketball Tournament.Ben Solomon/NCAA Photos via Getty ImagesBill Murray made the trip to Washington, D.C. Friday evening to watch UConn men's basketball take on Michigan State in the Sweet 16, likely one of the iconic actor's final times representing the Huskies behind Dan Hurley's bench. The 75-year-old actor was seated in the front row behind the Huskies' bench, wearing a navy blue vest and a UConn-branded hat. He was seated just a few rows in front of Bob Hurley Sr., the father of Hurley and a legendary high school basketball coach at New Jersey parochial school St. Anthony's.Article continues below this adGet Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.Get Digital Access and Stay Informed With Trusted Local News.ONLY 25¢Murray's son, Luke, has served as an assistant on the UConn coaching staff for the past five seasons, recognized as one of the sport's most respected tactical minds for his work crafting the Huskies' complex offensive scheme. Boston College announced Thursday that Murray has been hired as the school's next head basketball coach, the 40-year-old's first shot at leading a collegiate program. More For YouAn iconic American comedy actor, Murray first rose to prominence as a member of Saturday Night Live in the late 1970s, earning national acclaim on the silver screen from starring roles in \"Caddyshack\" and the \"Ghostbusters\" series. More recently, the 75-year-old actor has been a frequent collaborator with famed director Wes Anderson, working alongside him in films such as \"Fantastic Mr. Fox\" and \"Grand Budapest Hotel.\"Article continues below this adMurray has maintained deep ties to the Nutmeg State beyond his current stint at UConn. He was a two-sport athlete at St. Luke's School in New Canaan and enrolled at Fairfield University while he coached several AAU programs. His first collegiate coaching gig was offered by current Huskies general manager Tom Moore at Quinnipiac, where Murray served as the Bobcats' director of basketball operations.Should UConn advance past the second weekend, the Murray family's presence at the Final Four is still up in the air. According to a UConn spokesperson, there is no definitive answer from UConn yet on whether Luke Murray will remain with the Huskies or begin his tenure at Boston College. CT Insider LogoGet daily updates from the UConn basketball world.",
